<article class="about-page" webc:root="override">
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">About · Buenos Aires, Argentina</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Design perspective.<br />Engineering practice.</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">I’m Sebastian, a UI engineer who works between design systems, frontend architecture and accessible product experiences.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="page-section about-layout" aria-labelledby="story-title">
    <h2 id="story-title">01 / Story</h2>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>I started in graphic and product design, working on research, interaction flows and visual interfaces. Over time I moved closer to implementation because I wanted the final product to preserve the intent and care of the design.</p>
      <p>Today I build component libraries and design systems, translate tokens into resilient UI, and help designers and engineers make decisions together. I care about the details that make an interface feel clear, fast and dependable.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="principles" role="list">
      <li><strong>Clarity first</strong><p>Reduce ambiguity in the interface, the code and the conversations around both.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Systems over patches</strong><p>Create reusable foundations that let product teams move with confidence.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Accessibility by default</strong><p>Treat inclusive behavior as a core product requirement, not a final check.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section selected-work" aria-labelledby="selected-work-title">
